WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.569
-Senate Republicans,
with one notable exception,

00:00:03.569 --> 00:00:06.072
completed their cover-up
of the President's crimes today

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:08.308
when they acquitted him
after an impeachment trial

00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:09.542
with no witnesses.

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:11.444
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:11.444 --> 00:00:15.515
♪♪

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:17.483
Let's just say
it has not been a banner week

00:00:17.483 --> 00:00:19.118
for American democracy.

00:00:19.118 --> 00:00:21.120
First, of course,
there was the bizarre meltdown

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.922
at the Democratic Iowa caucus,
where an app designed

00:00:23.922 --> 00:00:26.693
to count people milling around
in high-school gymnasiums

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:28.962
crashed and delayed the results.

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:31.564
The app was built
by a company called Shadow,

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:34.033
which I assume is run
by Christoph waltz

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:36.202
from the Bond films.

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:38.037
[German accent] Shadow!

00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:40.140
And the crash resulted in chaos

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:43.075
on the ground
and on cable-news airwaves.

00:00:43.075 --> 00:00:45.378
-10:43 Eastern time.

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:46.913
-We still don't have
any results.

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:49.415
-We don't have any results
from Iowa.

00:00:49.415 --> 00:00:51.784
-Yeah, Brian, you know,
I've seen or texted with

00:00:51.784 --> 00:00:54.053
the Biden campaign manager
a few times tonight.

00:00:54.053 --> 00:00:56.789
And what does he keep saying to
me? "We don't know anything."

00:00:56.789 --> 00:00:59.458
-Of course, even if the app
worked perfectly,

00:00:59.458 --> 00:01:02.195
Joe Biden probably still
wouldn't know anything.

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:04.797
The only app Joe Biden
has ever used is FaceTime

00:01:04.797 --> 00:01:07.500
and only by accidentally
sitting on his phone.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.902
"Hello?! Hello?! Honey?!

00:01:09.902 --> 00:01:12.505
My wallet's
talking to me again!"

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:15.074
The chaos came after a day
of reporters roaming around

00:01:15.074 --> 00:01:17.076
high-school gyms in Iowa
and finding that Biden,

00:01:17.076 --> 00:01:18.578
once considered
the front-runner,

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:20.513
was having trouble
gaining traction.

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:22.982
-There was an entire
Biden segment.

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:26.619
Now it looks to be reduced to
just a very small corner here,

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:30.523
so certainly not
a robust turnout.

00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:33.359
-The Joe Biden group
probably not going to be viable.

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:37.596
-This is the Joe Biden
section here. Not too much.

00:01:37.596 --> 00:01:39.399
-This is the Bernie group.

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:42.702
It's so big that, in fact,
that middle section right there,

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:45.838
with all those folks in it,
that was the Joe Biden section.

00:01:45.838 --> 00:01:47.640
And they actually moved
the Joe Biden section

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:49.875
because they didn't have room
for all the Bernie supporters

00:01:49.875 --> 00:01:51.177
that are showing up here.

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:52.645
-Biden,
how are we doing over here?

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:55.047
This does not look like
56 people.

00:01:55.047 --> 00:01:57.550
So the Biden group --

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:00.987
So, you're -- You look like
lovely, wonderful people,

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:03.589
but it doesn't look like you
made the viability threshold.

00:02:03.589 --> 00:02:06.091
-Not yet. There's time, honey.

00:02:06.091 --> 00:02:09.362
-There's time. This year?

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:11.530
-Damn!

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:14.033
Jake Tapper is walking around
with a microphone

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:17.803
sassing people
like he's Billy Eichner.

00:02:17.803 --> 00:02:20.005
Seriously, Tapper going around
sassing voters

00:02:20.005 --> 00:02:21.507
is a show I would watch.

00:02:21.507 --> 00:02:24.577
They could call it
"Tap That Sass."

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:27.446
Also, look at this group
of people caucusing for Biden.

00:02:27.446 --> 00:02:29.482
They don't exactly look like
they're voting.

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:30.783
They just look like they got

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:33.319
knocked out of
a game of dodgeball.

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:36.889
"I'm so bad at dodging."
"Yeah, me too."

00:02:36.889 --> 00:02:38.524
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.524 --> 00:02:40.659
Then yesterday,
the Iowa Democratic Party

00:02:40.659 --> 00:02:43.129
finally got around to
announcing partial results,

00:02:43.129 --> 00:02:45.264
leaving everyone
somehow even more confused

00:02:45.264 --> 00:02:46.799
about what was happening,

00:02:46.799 --> 00:02:49.102
resulting in a breathless
Steve Kornacki

00:02:49.102 --> 00:02:51.471
racing around the studio
trying to digest

00:02:51.471 --> 00:02:54.106
all of the number vomit
that was being dumped on him.

00:02:54.106 --> 00:02:55.541
-Got a lot of questions here.

00:02:55.541 --> 00:02:57.310
I got to dive into these
and see where these came from.

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:59.812
Not every county gets, you know,
state delegate equivalents

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:01.714
that are equal to the turnout.

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:03.115
Sanders -- 30%.

00:03:03.115 --> 00:03:04.850
Iowa City, Johnson County.

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:06.352
Sanders -- 33%.

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:08.154
Getting big numbers
in these places.

00:03:08.154 --> 00:03:10.556
I'm out of breath here. Sorry.

00:03:10.556 --> 00:03:13.826
-My God. Someone
get that man some oxygen.

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:16.728
Also, there are 49 states to go,
Kornacki!

00:03:16.728 --> 00:03:18.931
You got to pace yourself!

00:03:18.931 --> 00:03:22.301
You're going to need the paddles
by Super Tuesday.

00:03:22.301 --> 00:03:23.936
In case you thought
this couldn't get

00:03:23.936 --> 00:03:26.105
any more complicated,
it turns out the Iowa caucus

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:27.640
used some complicated math

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:29.442
similar to
the electoral-college system

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:31.277
in order to give more weight
to rural areas,

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:33.446
meaning you could
actually win more delegates

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:35.247
even while losing
the popular vote.

00:03:35.247 --> 00:03:38.751
-Buttigieg's campaign right now
is in the lead in this category,

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:40.887
state delegate equivalents.

00:03:40.887 --> 00:03:42.621
We've been saying
this is a bit like

00:03:42.621 --> 00:03:44.757
the electoral-college/
popular-vote thing

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:47.092
where there's the potential
for a split.

00:03:47.092 --> 00:03:51.463
And right now, with 62% of
the expected vote in in Iowa,

00:03:51.463 --> 00:03:52.932
that's what you're seeing.

00:03:52.932 --> 00:03:54.367
So, again,
the possibility here --

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:58.003
Very possible right now that
Buttigieg is going to hang on,

00:03:58.003 --> 00:03:59.906
win the state-delegate
equivalents.

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:02.241
That's the traditional way
these things have been decided.

00:04:02.241 --> 00:04:04.310
And that Sanders is going to
get to say, "Hey, look.

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:07.613
More people came out
to support me than Buttigieg."

00:04:07.613 --> 00:04:11.050
The thing that's taking him from
close to the lead, actually,

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:16.022
is that peculiar state-delegate
equivalent allocation formula.

00:04:16.022 --> 00:04:19.292
When you apply that,
Buttigieg takes the lead.

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:22.928
-Just give it to the person
who gets the most votes!

00:04:22.928 --> 00:04:24.497
Why?

00:04:24.497 --> 00:04:26.198
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:26.198 --> 00:04:28.167
Please answer me.

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:30.736
Why did "American Idol"

00:04:30.736 --> 00:04:34.473
have a better system
than actual America?

00:04:34.473 --> 00:04:35.507
And yet, while Bernie,

00:04:35.507 --> 00:04:37.342
who was actually leading
the popular vote,

00:04:37.342 --> 00:04:39.578
remained restrained,
Buttigieg flew to New Hampshire

00:04:39.578 --> 00:04:41.080
with more confidence.

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:43.215
-I don't know
how anybody declares victory

00:04:43.215 --> 00:04:45.151
before you have
an official statement

00:04:45.151 --> 00:04:46.452
as to the election results.

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:49.154
So we're not declaring victory.

00:04:49.154 --> 00:04:50.823
-They're not complete,

00:04:50.823 --> 00:04:54.327
but results are in
from a majority of precincts,

00:04:54.327 --> 00:04:57.997
and they show our campaign
in first place.

00:04:57.997 --> 00:04:59.932
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:59.932 --> 00:05:02.234
-Hey, man, you can't just
declare yourself in first place

00:05:02.234 --> 00:05:03.436
when all the results aren't in

00:05:03.436 --> 00:05:04.904
and you're not even winning
the popular vote.

00:05:04.904 --> 00:05:07.106
That's not how it works.
If that were the case,

00:05:07.106 --> 00:05:09.608
then I could just declare myself
"People's" Sexiest Man Alive

00:05:09.608 --> 00:05:11.043
right now.

00:05:11.043 --> 00:05:13.646
And do you know --

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:19.118
do you know how pissed
Adam Driver would be?

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:22.888
Probably not at all
because we're basically twins.

00:05:22.888 --> 00:05:25.691
Also, I love the contrast
between how polished Pete is

00:05:25.691 --> 00:05:27.593
and the fact that Bernie
is doing his press conference

00:05:27.593 --> 00:05:30.029
on an airplane,
apparently in coach.

00:05:30.029 --> 00:05:32.565
"These seats are too roomy!
Who needs this much space?!

00:05:32.565 --> 00:05:35.234
I'm going to sit
in that over there overhead!"

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:37.770
[ Laughter ]

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:40.873
[ Applause ]

00:05:40.873 --> 00:05:44.510
"Pass me some pretzels!"

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:47.513
So, that was the state
of democracy on Monday.

00:05:47.513 --> 00:05:49.281
Then, last night,
an impeached president,

00:05:49.281 --> 00:05:51.817
who lost the popular vote, gave
the State of the Union address

00:05:51.817 --> 00:05:54.286
in which he demonized immigrants
and lied repeatedly

00:05:54.286 --> 00:05:58.056
from job numbers to immigration
to tax cuts to drug prices.

00:05:58.056 --> 00:06:00.325
For example, at one point,
Trump called on Congress

00:06:00.325 --> 00:06:02.461
to pass a bill to lower
prescription-drug prices,

00:06:02.461 --> 00:06:04.997
a bill Democrats have already
passed in the House

00:06:04.997 --> 00:06:06.232
and which Mitch McConnell

00:06:06.232 --> 00:06:07.800
has refused to take up
in the Senate.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:10.670
The bill is called HR3,
and some Democrats started

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:14.273
chanting the bill's name
in response to Trump's lie.

00:06:14.273 --> 00:06:16.876
-I'm calling
for bipartisan legislation

00:06:16.876 --> 00:06:19.511
that achieves the goal
of dramatically lowering

00:06:19.511 --> 00:06:22.247
prescription drug prices.

00:06:22.247 --> 00:06:23.582
Get a bill on my desk,

00:06:23.582 --> 00:06:26.552
and I will sign it into law
immediately.

00:06:26.552 --> 00:06:28.688
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:28.688 --> 00:06:31.090
-HR 3! HR 3!

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:34.293
-With unyielding commitment...

00:06:34.293 --> 00:06:36.061
-I love that
they're chanting the bill's name

00:06:36.061 --> 00:06:38.164
because you know Trump
has no idea what that means.

00:06:38.164 --> 00:06:39.565
[ Laughter ]

00:06:39.565 --> 00:06:43.069
"HR?
Wait. What?

00:06:43.069 --> 00:06:46.405
Isn't that where women file
all their complaints about me?

00:06:46.405 --> 00:06:48.808
I thought there
were way more than three."

00:06:48.808 --> 00:06:50.243
[ Laughter ]

00:06:50.243 --> 00:06:52.578
As is always the case with
Trump, there were so many lies,

00:06:52.578 --> 00:06:54.147
it was impossible to keep track,

00:06:54.147 --> 00:06:56.949
and the constant stream of lies
from Trump prompted glares

00:06:56.949 --> 00:06:58.551
of disapproval from Democrats,

00:06:58.551 --> 00:07:00.720
bewilderment from
House Speaker Nancy Pelosi,

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:04.289
and a solemn head shake
from Congressman Jim Clyburn.

00:07:04.289 --> 00:07:06.125
That face really sums it up
right there.

00:07:06.125 --> 00:07:08.861
That's the face you make
when your daughter tells you

00:07:08.861 --> 00:07:11.130
she's engaged
to a philosophy major.

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:12.564
[ Laughter ]

00:07:12.564 --> 00:07:14.867
"How are you gonna eat?"

00:07:14.867 --> 00:07:17.803
Compare that to the reactions
of Republicans in the crowd,

00:07:17.803 --> 00:07:19.705
like smirking
'80s movie villains

00:07:19.705 --> 00:07:21.774
Neil Gorsuch
and Brett Kavanaugh.

00:07:21.774 --> 00:07:24.743
And a horrifying smile from

00:07:24.743 --> 00:07:26.445
Senate Majority Leader
Mitch McConnell,

00:07:26.445 --> 00:07:31.117
who looked like Chucky
pretending he's not possessed.

00:07:31.117 --> 00:07:35.254
"Well, I'm just a --
I'm just a regular old doll.

00:07:35.254 --> 00:07:37.990
You can go to bed now.
I'm not, uh...

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:39.892
I'm not gonna do evil
once you sleep."

00:07:39.892 --> 00:07:41.526
[ Laughter ]

00:07:41.526 --> 00:07:43.361
Go to bed.

00:07:43.361 --> 00:07:44.997
Just a regular doll."

00:07:44.997 --> 00:07:46.132
[ Laughter ]

00:07:46.132 --> 00:07:48.267
Those two moments
are perfect illustrations

00:07:48.267 --> 00:07:50.570
of the crisis to democracy
we're currently facing.

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:52.671
A majority leader,
who actually represents

00:07:52.671 --> 00:07:54.707
a minority of Americans,
working with a president

00:07:54.707 --> 00:07:56.809
who lost the popular vote
by 3 million,

00:07:56.809 --> 00:07:58.344
installed two
Supreme Court justices

00:07:58.344 --> 00:07:59.678
with lifetime appointments.

00:07:59.678 --> 00:08:03.216
Now, every President uses
the State of the Union address

00:08:03.216 --> 00:08:04.417
to do a little campaigning,

00:08:04.417 --> 00:08:06.252
but Trump turned it
into a full-on rally.

00:08:06.252 --> 00:08:08.521
At one point, Republicans
literally started chanting

00:08:08.521 --> 00:08:09.789
"Four more years."

00:08:09.789 --> 00:08:12.724
-Four more years!
Four more years!

00:08:12.724 --> 00:08:16.161
Four more years!
Four more years!

00:08:16.161 --> 00:08:18.297
-Cool. The State of the Union
just turned into a Trump rally.

00:08:18.297 --> 00:08:21.033
I mean, the only difference
is Trump is squinting his way

00:08:21.033 --> 00:08:22.601
through a speech
someone else wrote for him

00:08:22.601 --> 00:08:25.371
instead of riffing
about insane stuff like this.

00:08:25.371 --> 00:08:31.210
-Sinks, toilets, and showers.

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:32.878
You don't get any water.

00:08:32.878 --> 00:08:36.448
-Four less flushes!
Four less flushes!

00:08:36.448 --> 00:08:39.351
And the undying devotion
most Republicans have pledged

00:08:39.351 --> 00:08:41.753
to a shameless, corrupt liar
was on full display today

00:08:41.753 --> 00:08:44.123
when they acquitted him
after a sham impeachment trial,

00:08:44.123 --> 00:08:45.458
in which
they ignored the evidence

00:08:45.458 --> 00:08:47.226
and refused
to hear from witnesses.

00:08:47.226 --> 00:08:48.761
A senate Republican caucus,

00:08:48.761 --> 00:08:51.096
again representing
a minority of Americans,

00:08:51.096 --> 00:08:53.232
acquitted a president
who lost the popular vote

00:08:53.232 --> 00:08:54.866
in the 2016 election

00:08:54.866 --> 00:08:56.669
and tried to cheat
in the 2020 election.

00:08:56.669 --> 00:08:58.504
You can't call that democracy.

00:08:58.504 --> 00:09:00.606
I mean, you could,
but then Jim Clyburn

00:09:00.606 --> 00:09:02.875
would give you this look again.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:02.875 --> 00:09:04.843
The only Republican who shocked
Washington today

00:09:04.843 --> 00:09:06.512
by announcing he would vote
to convict Trump

00:09:06.512 --> 00:09:09.181
and remove him from office,
was Utah Senator Mitt Romney.

00:09:09.181 --> 00:09:10.682
Romney announced his decision

00:09:10.682 --> 00:09:13.419
in both a floor speech
and on Fox News.

00:09:13.419 --> 00:09:17.223
-Were I to ignore the evidence
that has been presented

00:09:17.223 --> 00:09:18.791
and disregard what I believe

00:09:18.791 --> 00:09:21.560
my oath and the Constitution
demands of me,

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:25.530
for the sake of a partisan end,
it would, I fear,

00:09:25.530 --> 00:09:28.534
expose my character
to history's rebuke

00:09:28.534 --> 00:09:31.303
and the censure
of my own conscience.

00:09:31.303 --> 00:09:33.272
Applying impartial justice said

00:09:33.272 --> 00:09:36.442
what the President did
was grievously wrong,

00:09:36.442 --> 00:09:37.776
and I had to vote,

00:09:37.776 --> 00:09:39.511
if I was gonna live
with my own conscience,

00:09:39.511 --> 00:09:42.114
in a way that was consistent
with that oath of office.

00:09:42.114 --> 00:09:43.882
-First of all,
I love he did it on Fox News

00:09:43.882 --> 00:09:45.918
just to enrage Trump even more.

00:09:45.918 --> 00:09:49.121
Trump's aides probably had
to put duct tape over the TV

00:09:49.121 --> 00:09:51.524
to make the headline say, "Trump
is a good boy, and I love him."

00:09:51.524 --> 00:09:52.725
[ Laughter ]

00:09:52.725 --> 00:09:54.559
Second, it's shocking
just to hear a Republican

00:09:54.559 --> 00:09:56.095
talk about
living with their conscience.

00:09:56.095 --> 00:09:57.897
Most Republicans
filed for divorce

00:09:57.897 --> 00:09:59.265
from their consciences
years ago.

00:09:59.265 --> 00:10:01.634
That's why Mitch McConnell
is always smiling like that.

00:10:01.634 --> 00:10:02.868
[ Laughter ]

00:10:02.868 --> 00:10:04.369
"I do have a conscience.

00:10:04.369 --> 00:10:05.871
I'm not a haunted doll."

00:10:05.871 --> 00:10:07.473
[ Laughter ]

00:10:07.473 --> 00:10:08.707
"Go to bed."

00:10:08.707 --> 00:10:10.275
[ Laughter ]

00:10:10.275 --> 00:10:13.812
But while Romney was standing
alone among Republicans,

00:10:13.812 --> 00:10:16.349
the rest of his colleagues,
who voted to acquit Trump,

00:10:16.349 --> 00:10:19.117
were busy making excuses and
actually trying to convince us

00:10:19.117 --> 00:10:21.119
that Trump
won't just try to cheat again.

00:10:21.119 --> 00:10:23.288
Here's Maine Senator
Susan Collins

00:10:23.288 --> 00:10:24.824
explaining her vote yesterday.

00:10:24.824 --> 00:10:27.126
-Are you confident
that the President

00:10:27.126 --> 00:10:30.196
won't seek
foreign assistance again?

00:10:30.196 --> 00:10:35.033
-I believe that the President
has learned from this case.

00:10:35.033 --> 00:10:37.269
-What do you believe
the President has learned?

00:10:37.269 --> 00:10:39.972
-The President
has been impeached.

00:10:39.972 --> 00:10:42.041
That's a pretty big lesson.

00:10:42.041 --> 00:10:43.141
-Are you insane?

00:10:43.141 --> 00:10:45.010
Donald Trump
doesn't learn lessons.

00:10:45.010 --> 00:10:47.412
He's like an untrained dog.

00:10:47.412 --> 00:10:49.681
If he pees on the floor,
you got to rub his nose in it.

00:10:49.681 --> 00:10:51.750
And even then,
he'll probably do it again

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:53.886
while making
direct eye contact with you.

00:10:53.886 --> 00:10:55.754
[ Laughter ]

00:10:55.754 --> 00:10:59.858
Collins' argument falls on
the heels of Tennessee Senator

00:10:59.858 --> 00:11:02.961
Lamar Alexander, who made
a similar argument on Sunday.

00:11:02.961 --> 00:11:04.496
-Are you at all concerned,
though,

00:11:04.496 --> 00:11:06.298
when you seek
foreign interference --

00:11:06.298 --> 00:11:09.135
He does not believe
he's done anything wrong.

00:11:09.135 --> 00:11:10.569
That what has happened here

00:11:10.569 --> 00:11:13.171
might encourage him
that he can continue to do this?

00:11:13.171 --> 00:11:15.006
-I don't think so.
I hope not.

00:11:15.006 --> 00:11:17.309
I mean, enduring an impeachment

00:11:17.309 --> 00:11:19.045
is something
that nobody should like.

00:11:19.045 --> 00:11:21.313
Even the President said he
didn't want that on his résumé.

00:11:21.313 --> 00:11:22.581
I don't blame him.

00:11:22.581 --> 00:11:26.685
So, if a call like that
gets you an impeachment,

00:11:26.685 --> 00:11:29.455
I would think you would think
twice before he did it again.

00:11:29.455 --> 00:11:31.823
-What did his -- What --
What example

00:11:31.823 --> 00:11:34.893
in the life of Donald Trump,
has he been chastened?

00:11:34.893 --> 00:11:35.994
-[ Chuckles ]

00:11:35.994 --> 00:11:38.196
I haven't studied his life
that close.

00:11:38.196 --> 00:11:40.065
-Yeah, you don't have to
study his life

00:11:40.065 --> 00:11:41.967
because he's been in tabloids
and on reality TV

00:11:41.967 --> 00:11:43.402
for like 40 years.

00:11:43.402 --> 00:11:46.105
Everyone knows every intimate
detail of his personal life.

00:11:46.105 --> 00:11:48.240
If Donald Trump could strap
a GoPro to his head

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:50.809
and livestream every moment of
his life, he'd probably do it.

00:11:50.809 --> 00:11:53.745
Except it would suck because
all we'd see is Fox News,

00:11:53.745 --> 00:11:56.248
fast food, golf balls
slicing out of bounds,

00:11:56.248 --> 00:11:58.817
and women from the neck down.
[ Laughter ]

00:11:58.817 --> 00:12:00.186
"HR 4."

00:12:00.186 --> 00:12:01.987
[ Laughter ]

00:12:01.987 --> 00:12:04.156
This week
has showcased in vivid terms

00:12:04.156 --> 00:12:06.091
the crisis of democracy
we're facing.

00:12:06.091 --> 00:12:07.425
With the exception
of Mitt Romney,

00:12:07.425 --> 00:12:10.228
a Republican caucus representing
a minority of Americans

00:12:10.228 --> 00:12:11.896
acquitted a corrupt
Republican President

00:12:11.896 --> 00:12:13.265
who lost the popular vote

00:12:13.265 --> 00:12:15.334
and lied repeatedly in his
State of the Union address.

00:12:15.334 --> 00:12:17.502
Republicans are devoted to Trump
above all else,

00:12:17.502 --> 00:12:19.838
and they're willing to flush
both our democracy

00:12:19.838 --> 00:12:21.807
and our Constitution
down multiple...

00:12:21.807 --> 00:12:23.008
-Toilets!

00:12:23.008 --> 00:12:24.610
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:12:24.610 --> 00:12:28.414
[ Cheers and applause ]

